  m_text: "Rain is many short streaks falling at 9 m/s. Each drop is born in a flat box high above the ground. Its lifetime is set so it dies exactly at the ground; at its death a Sub Emitter starts one to three splashes. Stretched Billboard draws each drop as a streak along its motion.\n\n<size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: The Gas-Station sample (gd1), \xA7 12 \xB7 The rain.</color></size>"
