  m_text: 'A drip is one drop now and then. Emission has no steady rate, only a Burst of one drop every 0.8 seconds. The Burst''s Probability is below 1, so the rhythm is irregular. Gravity pulls the drop down. The Collision module stops it at the floor, where a Sub Emitter starts a splash.


    <size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: Unity Manual: Emission module, Collision module.</color></size>'
